ccpa_delete.body:
Hello {{broker_name}} privacy team,

I'm a California resident. Under the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the CPRA (Cal. Civ. Code §1798.105 and §1798.120), I'm asking you to:

1. Delete all personal information you hold about me, and tell your service providers and contractors to do the same.
2. Stop selling or sharing my personal information.

The details you need to find my records:

- Name: {{full_name}}
- Address: {{street_address}}, {{city}}, {{region}} {{postal_code}}
- Listing URLs (if any): {{profile_urls}}

The law gives you 45 days to respond, and 15 business days to act on the opt-out of sale or sharing. Please confirm by email at {{email}} when both are done. If you deny any part of this request, tell me which part and why.

If you're a registered data broker, you also have to process deletion requests sent through the California Delete Request and Opt-out Platform (DROP).

Thank you,
{{full_name}}
{{date}}

ccpa_opt_out.body:
Hello {{broker_name}} privacy team,

I'm a California resident. Under Cal. Civ. Code §1798.120 I'm opting out of the sale and sharing of my personal information, and under §1798.121 I'm asking you to limit the use of any sensitive personal information about me.

- Name: {{full_name}}
- City and state: {{city}}, {{region}}
- Email: {{email}}

The regulations give you 15 business days to act on this request. Please confirm by email when it's done.

Thank you,
{{full_name}}
{{date}}

eu_gdpr_erasure.body:
Hello {{broker_name}} data protection officer,

I live in {{country}}. Under the General Data Protection Regulation I'm asking you to:

1. Erase all personal data you hold about me without undue delay (Article 17).
2. Treat this as my objection to any processing for direct marketing or based on legitimate interests (Article 21).
3. Tell every recipient you disclosed my data to about this erasure (Article 19).

The details you need to find my records:

- Name: {{full_name}}
- City and country: {{city}}, {{country}}
- Listing URLs (if any): {{profile_urls}}

Article 12(3) gives you one month to respond. Please confirm in writing at {{email}}. If you refuse, tell me why and confirm my right to complain to a supervisory authority.

Thank you,
{{full_name}}
{{date}}

pipeda_withdraw.body:
Hello {{broker_name}} privacy officer,

I live in Canada. Under the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA), Schedule 1, Principle 4.3.8, I withdraw any consent to your collection, use or disclosure of my personal information. Under Principles 4.5.3 and 4.9, I'm asking you to:

1. Delete or anonymize the personal information you hold about me, including any listing on your website.
2. Stop disclosing or selling it to anyone else.
3. Tell me which personal information you held, where you got it, and who you disclosed it to.

The details you need to find my records:

- Name: {{full_name}}
- City and province: {{city}}, {{region}}
- Listing URLs (if any): {{profile_urls}}

PIPEDA gives you 30 days to respond to the access part of this request. Please confirm in writing at {{email}}. If you don't resolve this, I may file a complaint with the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada.

Thank you,
{{full_name}}
{{date}}

quebec_cessation.body:
Bonjour,

Je réside au Québec. En vertu de la Loi sur la protection des renseignements personnels dans le secteur privé, telle que modifiée par la Loi 25, je vous demande :

1. de cesser de diffuser mes renseignements personnels et de désindexer tout hyperlien rattaché à mon nom (article 28.1);
2. de supprimer les renseignements personnels que vous détenez à mon sujet (article 28);
3. de me dire quels renseignements vous déteniez, d'où ils proviennent et à qui vous les avez communiqués (article 27).

Les renseignements nécessaires pour retrouver mon dossier :

- Nom : {{full_name}}
- Ville : {{city}}, Québec
- Adresses URL de mes fiches (le cas échéant) : {{profile_urls}}

La loi vous accorde 30 jours pour répondre. Merci de me confirmer par écrit à {{email}} lorsque ce sera fait. À défaut de réponse, je pourrai m'adresser à la Commission d'accès à l'information.

Merci,
{{full_name}}
{{date}}

